    "pressure": {
      "file": "cooling_tower_gearbox_pressure.glb",
      "title": "Speed down, torque up",
      "description": "Motor speed (≈ 1500 rpm) is reduced about 10:1 to fan speed (≈ 150 rpm): the spiral-bevel set (40/12 ≈ 3.3) turns the drive through 90° and the helical set (45/15 = 3) completes the reduction. Output torque ≈ input torque × ratio × efficiency, so the output shaft and its bearings are much heavier. Gearboxes are selected with a service factor (typically ≥ 2.0 for cooling-tower duty), run in a humid, often icing environment, and depend on correct oil level — hence the remote oil gauge outside the stack.",
      "render": "normal",
      "annotations": []
    }
