  "summary": "A cooling tower gearbox is a right-angle speed reducer. A spiral-bevel gear set turns the horizontal drive through 90° and a helical stage completes about a 10:1 reduction to the vertical fan shaft. It is splash-lubricated from an oil bath and designed for a wet, cycling environment.",
